menu "mqjs SKK Japanese input"

choice MQJS_SKK_DICT_WHERE
    prompt "Where the conversion dictionary lives"
    default MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_PARTITION
    help
        ONE dictionary, in ONE place. Both places are flash read through
        the MMU in place — no allocation, no load, and the same search
        speed (docs/skk-ime-design.md §6.6). What differs is what the
        space costs and what it takes to change it.

        The partition is the default because it does not compete with the
        code for the 6 MB app partition, holds up to 8.5 MB, and can be
        rewritten without rebuilding the firmware.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_NONE
    bool "nowhere — build without a dictionary"
    help
        skk.open() then finds nothing and throws, unless the app passes
        an explicit path to a file. Saves the whole image; right for a
        build that will never type Japanese.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_BUILTIN
    bool "in the firmware image (flash rodata)"
    help
        Linked into the app image with .incbin. Costs app partition space
        — with 1.66 MB free today, anything past M is tight — and
        changing the dictionary means rebuilding and re-flashing 4.5 MB.

        In exchange it can never go missing: the bootloader verifies the
        whole app image with SHA-256 on every boot, so skk.open() skips
        the CRC pass and takes 175 us instead of 197 ms.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_PARTITION
    bool "in the `jisyo` partition"
    help
        The default. `idf.py flash` writes it for you, at the offset the
        partition table gives; `idf.py app-flash` leaves it alone and the
        contents survive, so the everyday loop is unaffected.

        Nothing verifies a partition — it is outside the image the
        bootloader checks — so skk.open() runs a CRC32 over it once:
        197 ms for ML, 826 ms for L. Conversion speed is unaffected.

endchoice

choice MQJS_SKK_DICT_SIZE
    prompt "Which SKK-JISYO"
    depends on !MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_NONE
    default MQJS_SKK_DICT_M if MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_BUILTIN
    default MQJS_SKK_DICT_ML
    help
        From https://github.com/skk-dev/dict . The number that decides
        whether continuous Japanese writing works is the OKURI-ARI count,
        not the total: conjugated verbs and adjectives are looked up
        there, and M has 1,412 of them against ML's 4,349.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_S
    bool "S — 3,379 headings (117 KB), 998 okuri-ari"
    help
        Smallest. Conjugation is largely absent; useful mainly to prove
        the path works with the least flash.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_M
    bool "M — 8,346 headings (303 KB), 1,412 okuri-ari"
    help
        Everyday nouns. Conjugated forms often miss, and the personal
        dictionary fills the gap over time. The largest that leaves the
        app partition comfortable, so it is the default for a built-in
        dictionary.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_ML
    bool "ML — 48,750 headings (1.86 MB), 4,349 okuri-ari"
    help
        Where continuous Japanese writing starts to work, and the default
        for the partition. Built in it does link — measured 6,191,264 B
        against a 6 MB `factory` — but with 2% left, which the next
        feature spends.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_L
    bool "L — 175,790 headings (8.07 MB), 15,996 okuri-ari"
    depends on !MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_BUILTIN
    help
        Everything. Not offered for a built-in dictionary because it does
        not fit the 6 MB app partition at all. In the partition it costs
        ~34 s per `idf.py flash` and makes skk.open() 826 ms instead of
        197 ms — the CRC pass, nothing else. Conversion stays at 6 cache
        lines per lookup because the index is a sampled tree.

endchoice

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_SOURCE_DIR
    string "Directory holding SKK-JISYO.{S,M,ML,L}"
    default ""
    depends on !MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_NONE
    help
        Absolute, or relative to the project root. Set it and the build
        prepares the image with tools/skk_prep.py, which transcodes,
        RE-SORTS into UTF-8 byte order and verifies every entry before
        writing anything (the EUC-JP sort trap, §6.1).

        Empty means "do not regenerate": the prepared .bin in
        components/skk_core/ is used exactly as it is, and the build
        prints how many headings it actually holds rather than which one
        was selected here. That is the default because the source
        dictionaries are large, carry their own licence terms and are
        gitignored. With neither a source nor a .bin the build says so
        and still succeeds — a dictionary must not be what stops a fresh
        clone from flashing.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_STRIP_ANNOTATIONS
    bool "Strip ';annotation' from candidates"
    default n
    depends on !MQJS_SKK_DICT_AT_NONE
    help
        Drops the explanatory note some entries carry after ';'. Saves
        538 KB on L, almost nothing on M, and v1 does not display them
        anyway. Only acts when the image is regenerated.

endmenu
